  "description": "Perfect for feeding a crowd or fixing a solo meal on the fly, this simple home-style Taiwanese noodle-and-vegetable dish may look bland, but hidden within are layers of flavor, thanks to plenty of white pepper, black vinegar, and broth.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: vegetable oil → peanut oil\n\nNotes: Look for black vinegar and Taiwanese rice noodles, often labeled \"Hsinchu rice noodles,\" in Asian groceries. Otherwise, use the thinnest type of dried Asian rice noodle you can find.",
